DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_BB56_E69F';
<p>bb56_e69f</p> <p><strong>Deuteranomaly red-green color blindness </strong> is an X-linked recessive genetic disorder that is caused by mutations in the OPN1MW gene. This results in shift in the green retinal receptors toward red wavelength sensitivity. The disorder affects 1 in 20 males and 1 in 400 females of Northern European ancestry. Individuals affected with color blindness have decreased ability to see colors in which they are unable distinguish between shades of red and green. The defective gene for color blindness is located on the long arm of chromosome X at position 28. </p><p><strong>Achondroplasia </strong> is an autosomal dominant genetic disorder that is caused by a mutation in the FGFR3 gene. This results in a mutated protein that interacts negatively with growth factors leading to complications with bone production. The disorder affects 1 in 27,500 people. Individuals affected with achondroplasia have dwarfism with short arms and legs, an enlarged head, and a prominent forehead. The defective gene for achondroplasia is located on the short arm of chromosome 4 at position 16.3. </p><p>A man (&male;) with both color blindness and achondroplasia genetic disorders marries a wild-type phenotype woman (&female;) with neither disorder. The father (&male;) of the woman has the color blindness genetic disorder,but mother (&female;) of the woman does not. The father (&male;) of the man is wild-type phenotype and does not have the achondroplasia genetic disorder.</p> <p>Reminder: color blindness is X-linked recessive and achondroplasia is autosomal dominant.</p><p>What fraction of their daughters (&female;) will have both color blindness and achondroplasia genetic disorders?</p>
PROMPT_BB56_E69F
loadMacros('parserRadioButtons.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CHOICE_1';
None, 0%
LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CHOICE_2';
1/4, 25%
LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CHOICE_3';
1/2, 50%
LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CHOICE_4';
3/4, 75%
LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CHOICE_5';
All, 100%
LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CHOICE_5
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CORRECT_1';
1/4, 25%
LITERAL_BB56_E69F_CORRECT_1
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5);
$answer = RadioButtons([@choices], $correct_1, labels => 'ABC', displayLabels => 1, randomize => 0, noindex => 1, separator => '<div style="margin-bottom: 0.7em;"></div>');
TEXT(MODES(HTML => $prompt, TeX => ''));
BEGIN_TEXT
\{$answer->buttons\}
END_TEXT
